{"ts":"2026-08-28T15:59:27.509Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"7405dc9b453c8154184ac8fe","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-rust-yilr"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The release workflow pins a pm CLI three weeks older than CI's, and its changelog reads are bounded"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"This repository pins two different pm CLI versions. CI installs 2026.8.21 to run pm health with merge drivers required; the release workflow installs 2026.8.6 for all three of its pm-changelog invocations. That older pin is not neutral: its pm health invocation is known to hang, so any step that reaches for health inside the release job inherits a silent stall rather than a failure, and the two pins disagree about item hashing, which is what makes a history drift verdict depend on which binary produced it. Separately, none of the three invocations passes the unbounded output budget and output limit controls every other fleet package passes. pm-github proved that fuse is real: it kept releasing until its tracker reached eighty-six items, then failed for ten consecutive days on a read truncated to five."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:release","type:defect"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-28T15:59:27.509Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-28T15:59:27.509Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Both workflows install the same exact pm CLI version; every pm-changelog invocation in the release workflow requests a complete unbounded workspace read"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"18c5f90fcc6259934c2e23340aaa4b63268a4eb9e11f108fecbe0afebd7cf14f","item_hash_version":2,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
{"ts":"2026-08-28T16:00:17.177Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"7405dc9b453c8154184ac8fe","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-28T16:00:17.177Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-28T16:00:17.177Z","author":"claude","text":"Both workflows now install @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.21, and the release workflow's pm-changelog moves from 2026.8.6 to 2026.8.22 to match the rest of the fleet. All three invocations request a complete unbounded workspace read. The forwarding is proven rather than assumed: running the pinned generator with --pm-arg naming a flag pm does not have returns pm's own unknown_option error for that flag, so the arguments reach the binary and the controls are not inert."}]}],"before_hash":"18c5f90fcc6259934c2e23340aaa4b63268a4eb9e11f108fecbe0afebd7cf14f","after_hash":"a085d91534ffbcf7708d6035556ebc9aab0c858c94cae40ee5f15ec6c5c78183","item_hash_version":2,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
